+# Profile save and recovery
+
+This record owns the implementation plan and acceptance evidence for the existing
+React/TypeScript profile form. The public `ProfileForm({ profile })` and
+`updateProfile(displayName)` entry points remain unchanged. README.md supplies the
+product contract; no new service or library is needed.
+
+## Behavior and design
+
+Typing changes only the draft. Save snapshots that draft, publishes the name
+immediately and issues the existing PATCH request. Saving remains available while
+another request is pending. Success accepts the server's returned name; failure
+retains the draft, restores the latest confirmed name and shows
+`Save failed. Please retry.` in an alert. Save submits the currently edited draft
+again; there is no automatic write retry.
+
+Request sequence and profile version answer different questions. A local request
+ID determines which intent may publish success/error feedback. The numeric server
+version determines the newest confirmed fallback. An older response may advance
+that fallback while a newer name stays visible. An older failure cannot erase a
+newer pending or successful save. If the newest save fails before an older save
+succeeds, the later acknowledgement updates the fallback without hiding the error.
+Version is treated as the server revision; equal/lower versions do not replace an
+already confirmed revision. Client sequencing does not promise server commit order
+or resolve edits from other devices.
+
+The API is the external-data boundary: reject unsuccessful HTTP responses, JSON
+parsing errors and bodies whose id/displayName are not strings or whose version is
+not a finite number. The form catches these failures once and owns user feedback.
+It does not expose response details. A returned Profile is trusted inside the UI.
+
+The component owns the draft and PATCH effect. A small pure reducer owns atomic
+save transitions; visible name is derived, never independently synchronized.
+This is a local adaptation of React's reducer/unidirectional state flow and
+[stale-result lifecycle guidance](https://react.dev/learn/synchronizing-with-effects).
+No cache, class, request engine or form library is warranted for this one form.
+The inner editor is keyed by profile ID so replacing the resource discards its
+draft and pending publication. A server write is not undone on unmount; its old
+completion targets only the discarded editor. The supplied profile seeds the
+editor; background refreshing of the same resource is outside the current API.
+
+## Three ordered increments
+
+1. **Validate the acknowledgement.** Change `src/api.ts` without changing the
+   PATCH payload or exported signature. Completion requires HTTP errors, invalid
+   JSON/shape and valid responses to be exercised at the API and form boundaries.
+2. **Reconcile visible intent and confirmed state.** Add `src/profileSaveState.ts`
+   and update `src/ProfileForm.tsx`. Completion requires immediate display,
+   normalized successful names, latest failure rollback, both response orders,
+   superseded failure suppression, retained drafts and resource replacement.
+3. **Close acceptance and document evidence.** Add separate regression files,
+   preserve the supplied tests and manifests, run `npm run check`, inspect actual
+   declarations/callers and reconcile this record with the final result.
+
+## Implemented code contracts
+
+| Owner / operation | Contract and responsibility | Caller |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `api.ts` / `Profile` (existing) | `{ id: string; displayName: string; version: number }` | Form and reducer |
+| `api.ts` / `updateProfile(displayName: string): Promise<Profile>` (changed) | PATCH the snapshot; resolve only a validated successful acknowledgement, otherwise reject | Editor submit handler |
+| `api.ts` / `isProfile(value: unknown): value is Profile` (new, private) | Validate the external successful JSON body once | updateProfile |
+| `profileSaveState.ts` / `createProfileSaveState(profile: Profile): ProfileSaveState` (new) | Seed confirmed state with no submitted intent | Editor reducer initialization |
+| `profileSaveState.ts` / `profileSaveReducer(state: ProfileSaveState, action: ProfileSaveAction): ProfileSaveState` (new) | Submitted, accepted and rejected transitions; version-ordered fallback and request-ordered publication | React dispatch |
+| `profileSaveState.ts` / `getVisibleName(state: ProfileSaveState): string` (new) | Pending snapshot, newest accepted result or confirmed fallback after failure | Editor rendering |
+| `ProfileForm.tsx` / `ProfileForm({ profile }: { profile: Profile })` (existing) | Resource identity boundary; compose keyed editor | Public consumer |
+| `ProfileForm.tsx` / `ProfileEditor({ profile }: { profile: Profile })` (new, private) | Draft, request IDs, native submit handling, request effects and accessible feedback | ProfileForm |
+| `ProfileEditor` / `async function handleSubmit(event: FormEvent)` (changed, nested) | Prevent native navigation, snapshot draft, dispatch submitted, await updateProfile, dispatch accepted or rejected; captures the editor's draft, dispatch and request-ID ref | Native form onSubmit |
+
+`ProfileSaveState` contains the confirmed Profile and one latest intent, either
+pending with its snapshot, succeeded with its returned Profile, or failed. The
+latest intent's ID is retained after settlement to suppress older publication.
+There is no need to retain every request or duplicate the input inside a cache.
+
+## Technical architecture
+
+```text
+Public consumer
+    -- Profile seed --> ProfileForm [profile.id identity boundary]
+                          -- keyed mount --> ProfileEditor [draft + request effect]
+                                               | -- actions --> profileSaveReducer
+                                               | <-- state ----- [pure local model]
+                                               | -- state --> getVisibleName
+                                               | <-- name -----------------|
+                                               | -- snapshot --> updateProfile
+                                               |                  [HTTP + JSON validation]
+                                               |                     | PATCH /api/profile
+                                               |                     v
+                                               |                  External server
+                                               | <-- Profile or rejection --|
+                                               v
+                                    native form / current name / status / alert
+```
+
+## Data flow and recovery
+
+```text
+Type "Grace" --> editor draft only (current name stays "Ada")
+Save A --> capture "Grace", allocate ID 1 --> submitted --> visible "Grace"
+       --> updateProfile("Grace") --> PATCH --> validate acknowledgement
+Save B --> capture "Lin", allocate ID 2   --> submitted --> visible "Lin"
+       --> updateProfile("Lin")   --> PATCH --> validate acknowledgement
+  A success (version 2) --> accepted ID 1 --> confirmed "Grace"; keep visible "Lin"
+  B failure            --> rejected ID 2 --> visible confirmed "Grace" + alert
+                                            draft "Lin" remains editable
+  B succeeds first     --> accepted ID 2 --> visible returned B name, clear pending
+  A fails later        --> rejected ID 1 --> no visible/error change
+  B fails first        --> rejected ID 2 --> initial fallback + alert
+  A succeeds later     --> accepted ID 1 --> advance fallback, preserve alert
+  Replace profile ID   --> new keyed editor --> new seed and draft;
+                           old completions cannot publish into the new editor
+```
+
+Both diagrams use labelled plain text, so no diagram parser/toolchain is required.
+
+## Verification and evolution
+
+Checks use the real form with controllable fetch promises, not private
+request counters. They assert settled names, alerts, draft content and subsequent
+PATCH bodies. API tests cover valid and rejected responses. The supplied harness
+files and local skill remain read-only; separate test files provide extra cases.
+
+A realistic follow-up is adding another editable profile field. The API remains
+the validation boundary, the reducer remains the atomic confirmation/intent owner,
+and the editor can capture a typed draft object instead of a name. No general
+field registry or transport abstraction is needed today. Backend conflict
+resolution would require a service contract rather than a client-only queue.
+
+Baseline `npm run check` passed typechecking but failed two supplied tests before
+their save assertions because earlier renders remained mounted. Vitest globals are
+disabled, so Testing Library did not discover a global `afterEach` for automatic
+cleanup. `vitest.config.ts` now loads `src/testSetup.ts`, which explicitly registers
+`afterEach(cleanup)`. This repairs test isolation without editing the supplied
+harness or changing production behavior.
+
+All three increments are complete. Final `npm run check` passed TypeScript and all
+27 tests across three files (including the three unchanged supplied tests).
+
+| Increment / rule | Executed evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| 1 — validated PATCH acknowledgement | `api.test.ts`: exact PATCH request, valid return, HTTP error with valid-looking body, invalid field shapes, non-finite version, malformed JSON and transport rejection |
+| 2 — optimistic intent and rollback | Supplied `ProfileForm.test.tsx`: pending display, invalid-body rollback, older accepted fallback while latest save fails |
+| 2 — concurrent completion and draft ownership | `ProfileForm.recovery.test.tsx`: draft-only edit, normalized return without draft loss, both old-failure completion orders, late success after latest failure, lower-version suppression, server revision independent of client order |
+| 2 — recovery and lifecycle | `ProfileForm.recovery.test.tsx`: HTTP/JSON/network failure and explicit retry, profile-ID replacement for both success/failure, Enter submission and settled result |
+| 3 — integration and maintenance | `npm run check`; final declaration/caller search and code/document cross-read; `git diff --check`; protected-file SHA256 comparison |
+
+The final cross-read traced `handleSubmit` through validated `updateProfile`,
+reducer dispatch and `getVisibleName`, including the alert/status branches. It also
+checked keyed editor replacement. The declarations, call conventions and both
+diagrams describe these final owners. Adding a second field would change the
+typed draft/snapshot and Profile validation, while the acknowledgement ordering
+rule stays in the reducer; no extra architectural mechanism was added.
+
+The raw installation, baseline failure, successful check and integrity results are
+saved outside the workspace at the sibling path obtained by appending
+`-validation.log` to this workspace directory name. Reproduce with `npm ci` then
+`npm run check` (Node 22.22.2 was used; when needed, prepend
+`/Users/heguangwei/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin` to PATH).
+
+Verification uses Node/jsdom and controlled transport. There is no runnable
+application/server entry point in the supplied project, so no real browser,
+backend commit ordering or cross-device conflict behavior is claimed. `npm ci`
+reported four existing dependency audit findings (two moderate, two high); their
+applicability was not assessed, and the protected manifest/lockfile are unchanged.
